;; jukebox.ab3 -- the jukebox page (the jukebox plan, step 0): the sound's settings and every
;; song and effect on one page, with four characters from the game hopping to each channel's
;; loudness. Compile in UAE (execute sparky-dave:S/run-proof). Not part of the game.
;;
;; What it is built from: the game's own display (the HUD list over the dual playfield world
;; list, fetch mode 3, the back in front by PF2PRI over a blank front, the overlay's two 384 px
;; pages on the back bitmap, as proofs/overlay.ab3 proved), the game's own sound files (so what
;; is heard is what the game plays), the game's sheets and shape slots (#PRE_*), the HUD font.
;; Left out: the band split (the page does not scroll).
;;
;; The backdrop: the start of 1-1 (the hill, the bush, the ground) behind the stage, from the host
;; preview picture assets/world1-1-320x256.iff. It is on the FRONT playfield (the blank cover), drawn
;; once, so it costs no time per frame; the back page's pen 0 is transparent over it. The picture
;; has its own palette order, so the front uses its colours (front entries 1 to 8) and a spare pen
;; (9) for the sky behind the hill, filled first so that the picture's own sky (its pen 0) can be
;; transparent; entry 0 stays black, so the rest of the page is black and the text is readable. The
;; real feature would stamp the real map's cells with the atlas instead of using this picture.
;;
;; Questions it answers
;;   1. Cost. Each frame draws on the hidden page only what changed: a character that moved or
;;      changed frame (erased where it was, drawn where it is; the first version cleared the whole
;;      stage strip, 127 lines a frame, and the loop ran slower than the display: the music dragged
;;      and the keys lagged) and the rows that changed (a cursor move is two rows, a value one),
;;      each page keeping its own list. The results file gives the lines of the sound ticks, the
;;      stage, the rows and the whole frame's work, and the display frames that really passed
;;      against the loop's passes (CIA-A's time of day counts the vertical sync): they must match.
;;   2. Layout. A heading, a stage of about 80 px, nine rows at a 12 px pitch and a readout line in
;;      the view (rows 32 to 239). Look at it for fit and readability.
;;   3. The hop. Each character rises at once to a height from its channel's loudness
;;      (apuState #AP_LEVEL, times the group's volume step) and falls back under gravity. Does it
;;      look like the music? Do the volume rows change it? Does the layout row move the
;;      characters to the other side?
;;   4. The art. Mario (pulse 1), the Goomba (pulse 2), the Koopa (the triangle), the mushroom (the
;;      noise), blitted into the back bitmap: are the colours right?
;;   5. The engine's state can be saved and put back (F1 and F2), which leaving the page in a game
;;      will do so the game's music goes on where it was. Play the ground music, F1, play another
;;      song or an effect, F2: the ground music should carry on from the same place.
;;
;; Keys
;;   Up, Down   choose a row          Left, Right  change the row's value
;;   Return     SONG: play the song shown (the same one again: stop)   EFFECT: play it   DEFAULTS: the sound's defaults
;;   F1 save the engine's state       F2 put it back          F10  quit
;;   Esc        discard the changes made since the page opened (or since BACK last saved): the
;;              sound goes back as it was, nothing is written. A BACK row that has changes to save
;;              reads SAVE AND BACK, with ESC DISCARDS beside it; Return on it keeps them. On a
;;              CD32 pad red (A) is Return and blue (B) is Esc: the pad is not read here.
;; Rows: SONG, EFFECT, SOUND LAYOUT, FILTER, PULSE VOLUME, TRIANGLE VOLUME, NOISE VOLUME,
;; DEFAULTS, BACK (here it only takes the changes as saved: nothing is written).
;;
;; Writes jukebox-results.txt on exit.

WBStartup

XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.look.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.constants.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.physics.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.level.meta.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.sound.data.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.sound.ab3"

